al_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I couldn't do the main job of PKT-0041: nothing was measured. My permissions blocked running the installed `x2t` and even listing `/var/www/euro-office/documentserver/server/FileConverter/bin`, since only the worktree is allowed. I didn't try to get around that. So there are no per-phase timings, `baseline.md` is unchanged, and I make no claim about which phase dominates.\n\n**What I did instead** (committed as e500a3d; `theseus validate` reports 0 errors; the packet has no acceptance commands):\n- **Source analysis:** I read the pipeline in `external/core` and wrote it up in `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0041-x2t-pdf-split.md`.\n  - Each `x2t` run creates a new `CDoctrenderer` and V8 context, so nothing is reused between conversions.\n  - The sdkjs scripts load from a precompiled snapshot (`sdkjs/<editor>/sdk-all.bin`) only if the build has snapshot support and that file exists. Otherwise the large `sdk-all-min.js`, `AllFonts.js` and `sdk-all.js` are compiled on every run, with an optional `sdk-all.cache` code cache.\n  - If building the snapshots fails, the error only goes to stderr (`doctrenderer.cpp:1105`), so the slow path is easy to miss.\n- **Hypothesis to check:** the 0.65 s for an empty docx→pdf, against 70 ms for ODF, is probably mostly V8 startup and script loading. If the package ships no snapshots, the P3 fix may just be generating them at install time with `x2t -create-js-snapshots`. If it does, most of the time is in sdkjs layout, and the \"under 20 % fixed cost\" downgrade rule in DIAG-x2t applies.\n- **Measurement script:** `.theseus/oracle/perf/x2t-split.sh` splits a conversion into phases using strace timestamps. It is an untested draft.\n- **Follow-up request:** in `.theseus/spawn/`, with `requires: [documentserver]`, to run the script on the empty templates, the PKT-0016 samples and a save conversion.\n- **Packet notes:** the Executor log, Lessons for the Atlas and the friction line are written.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- How sdkjs loads (snapshot, else full compile with an optional code cache) and the silent snapshot failure belong on the x2t card.\n- Packets that measure the installed stack need `requires: [documentserver]` and access to `/var/www/euro-office`. `environment.md` says measurement packets run with every privilege, but this session didn't have them.\n\n**Decision for you:** the follow-up can only produce numbers if its session is allowed to execute `x2t` and `strace`/`perf` and read `/var/www/euro-office`.","ttft_ms":1755,"type":"result","duration_ms":75954,"uuid":"85a7d5b3-1be2-4309-a6ac-1b2b59c1edfc","ttft_stream_ms":771,"time_to_request_ms":170,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":59,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":6,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":12,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":21,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":1,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":67,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":145,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":217,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":142,"process_rss_mib_result":232,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_peak_rss_mib":261,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3210,"process_wall_ms_turn":75953,"process_cpu_m